# fn? narrowing in the false branch: the variable gets type Negation(any-function),
# i.e., "definitely not a function". Calling such a value in the false branch
# produces a type warning: "expected function type, got ~Fn@_ [ ...]".
#
# At runtime, x IS a function so fn? returns true and the false branch is never
# executed — eval succeeds and returns "is-a-function". The type warning comes
# from the static false-branch analysis (fn-narrowing-variadic sprint).
[x: [fn [let a] a]
 result: [if [fn? x] "is-a-function" [x 1]]]
=== out
Dict({"x": Function(a), "result": String("is-a-function")})
=== warn
expected function type, got ~Fn@_
